   "year_over_year_estimate": "about 6x (latest quarterly growth of 1.57x compounded over four quarters). A measured year-over-year figure is not possible: AI logging starts in 2025Q4 and stops 2026-06-30.",
   "working_assumption_for_ladder": "Machine maths capability is moving up about one difficulty tier every 6 to 9 months: modest Erdos problems in late 2025, dozens per quarter by mid 2026, a claimed Millennium Prize problem (Navier-Stokes) in September 2026. Volume on the Erdos list is now limited by human checking and by the shrinking pool of easier problems, not by machine output."
  },
  "method": "1) Rebuilt every problem's status at each of 1,699 commits of problems.yaml; counted the last move from an open-type status into proved, disproved or solved for problems still solved on 2026-11-22. 2) Parsed all 538 rows of the AI contributions wiki; 'new proof' = sections 1a to 1d with a full-solution (green) outcome, 'found existing literature' = section 2a with a full-solution outcome; counted unique problems by date of first such entry. 3) Joined the two to label status changes. 4) Rate = last full logged quarter; growth = half over half and latest quarter over quarter compounded. Scripts: /home/claude/e2v5/scripts/parse_wiki.py, transitions.py, trans_count2.py, pace_counts.py.",
  "caveats": [
   "The wiki stopped on 2026-06-30, so AI attribution for 2026Q3 and 2026Q4 cannot be verified from the logged list.",
   "On 2026-10-06 erdosproblems.com stopped showing statuses and solved counts; status updates now lag behind claims, so the 2026Q3 and 2026Q4 all-cause counts understate machine output.",
   "The wiki says it is not a benchmark and has selection bias: easy or obscure problems fall first; absence of past progress can reflect obscurity rather than difficulty.",
   "Status history contains same-day flip-flops (a status set then reverted); the count uses the last entry into a solved state, which removes those.",
   "The April 2026 spike (30) reflects a batch of results from new OpenAI models, so quarterly numbers are lumpy.",
   "Several big claims (OpenAI 100+ problems, Tier 4 97.6%) are company reports not independently checked."
